Theorem RL-9: explicit and compact sharing observations select identical outcomes

  Preconditions:
    - RL-7 freezes a SharingObservationRequired obligation.
    - A projection may encode the observation explicitly or compactly.

  Soundness property:
    Forall sharing-observation result r:
      (P1) explicit_observation_outcome(r) = compact_observation_outcome(r).
      (P2) one owner selects SameIdentityAdmissible and multiple owners select
           IsolationRequired.
      (P3) both outcomes preserve evaluator value semantics when satisfied.
    The theorem does not freeze a diamond, branch, compound instruction, copy,
    or sharing-observation mechanism.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate both observation results:
      one_owner_observed = true -> SameIdentityAdmissible
      one_owner_observed = false -> IsolationRequired
    Coverage gate: 2 results with explicit/compact equality and soundness.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl9_cow_compound_contraction)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
